SUMMARY:Panigiri of Profitis Ilias\, Profitis Ilias village
LOCATION:Profitis Ilias\, Samothrace\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The mountain village of Profitis Ilias in the south-west\, famous for its goat tavernas\, keeps its patron's day on 20 July with gorgovrasto after the liturgy\, dancing\, and roast goat in the evening. The island's best-known panigiri for food\; the tavernas are packed\, so eat at the communal tables or book.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samothrace/#profitis-ilias-panigiri-of-profitis-ilias-profitis-ilias-vil
